## Graphic Abstract
## Highlights：
A novel support based on CdS quantum dots was proposed for UiO66- $(\mathrm{SH})_{2}$ -CdS hybrids.   
CdS quantum dots were connected to the UiO-66- $(\mathrm{SH})_{2}$ by thiol group.   
The as-prepared UiO-66- $(\mathrm{SH})_{2}$ -CdS0.7 showed superior photocatalytic performance for $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ evolution.   
UiO66- $(\mathrm{SH})_{2}$ -CdS hybrids exhibit high stability and reusability during the catalytic reaction.   
Efficient charge separation and transfer were observed in the composites.
